<!DOCTYPE html>
<html data-framework="lit"><head>
        <meta charset="utf-8">
        <title>TodoMVC: Lit</title>
        <script async="" src="https://www.google-analytics.com/analytics.js"></script><script type="module" src="./index.js"></script>
        <style>
            html,
            body {
                margin: 0;
                padding: 0;
            }
            body {
                font: 14px "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
                line-height: 1.4em;
                background: #f5f5f5;
                color: #111111;
                min-width: 230px;
                max-width: 550px;
                margin: 0 auto;
                -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
                -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
                font-weight: 300;
            }
            .info {
                margin: 65px auto 0;
                color: #4d4d4d;
                font-size: 11px;
                text-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
                text-align: center;
            }
            .info p {
                line-height: 1;
            }
            .info a {
                color: inherit;
                text-decoration: none;
                font-weight: 400;
            }
            .info a:hover {
                text-decoration: underline;
            }
        </style>
		<link rel="stylesheet" href="./base.css">
    </head>
    <body class="learn-bar"><aside class="learn"><header> <h3>Lit</h3> <span class="source-links">   <h5>Example</h5> <a href="https://github.com/tastejs/todomvc/tree/gh-pages/examples/lit">Source</a>   </span> </header> <hr> <blockquote class="quote speech-bubble"> <p>Lit is a simple library for building fast, lightweight web components. It pairs reactive properties and declarative HTML templates with the standard Custom Elements and Shadow DOM APIs, so components are first-class browser citizens that work across any framework or none.</p> <footer> <a href="http://lit.dev">Lit</a> </footer> </blockquote>  <hr>  <h4>Official Resources</h4> <ul>  <li> <a href="https://lit.dev/docs/getting-started/">Getting Started</a> </li>  <li> <a href="https://lit.dev/tutorials/">Tutorials</a> </li>  </ul>   <footer> <hr> <em>If you have other helpful links to share, or find any of the links above no longer work, please <a href="https://github.com/tastejs/todomvc/issues">let us know</a>.</em> </footer></aside>
        <todo-app></todo-app>
        <footer class="info">
            <p>Double-click to edit a todo</p>
            <p>Written by <a href="https://github.com/lit">the lit team</a></p>
            <p>Part of <a href="http://todomvc.com">TodoMVC</a></p>
        </footer>
		<script src="./base.js"></script>
    

</body></html>
